<h1>Duplicate registration review</h1>

<p class="tw:mt-4">
  Review groups of live registrations with the same whole normalized serial and
  manufacturer. Counts below are groups and registration records, not
  comparisons or confirmed duplicate bicycles. Serials shorter than six
  characters and partial matches remain in the
  <%= link_to "serial-segment view", admin_duplicate_bikes_path(search_view: "segments"), class: "twlink" %>.
</p>

<p class="tw:mt-4 tw:font-bold">
  Review only. No merging, deletion or customer emails. A stolen report anywhere
  on a matching whole serial, including recovered, deleted and test records,
  puts the group in Stolen history. Preserve those records separately.
</p>

<p class="tw:mt-4">
  Test markers include the administrators organization and designated test
  contact in current or historical links. These markers identify a review scope,
  not permission to delete. Groups of
  <%= BikeServices::DuplicateReviewFinder::LARGE_GROUP_MINIMUM %> or more need
  serial validation; repeated entries may contain a placeholder or product code.
  Shop followed by customer requires exactly two entries, an earlier POS entry
  and a later customer-channel entry. It does not establish that the customer
  registered it personally or owns both entries.
</p>

<p class="tw:mt-4">
  Strongest evidence additionally requires the same known initial email and
  account, a claimed self-registration by the customer, an unclaimed shop entry,
  matching current identities, compatible known model/year and original serials,
  and no transfers, impound, marketplace or generic "Other" manufacturer. Photos
  and stickers still need preservation. Different emails and spelling
  similarities belong in manual review; they do not authorize an email or merge.
</p>

<p class="tw:mt-4">
  Counts computed
  <%= render UI::Time::Component.new(time: @group_snapshot[:generated_at]) %>.
  Cached for up to one hour. Stolen history is checked again when a comparison
  opens.
</p>

<% kinds = BikeServices::DuplicateReviewFinder::KINDS %>
<% summary = @summary %>
<% active_kind = @kind %>

<%= render UI::Table::Component.new(records: kinds.to_a) do |table| %>
  <% table.column(label: "Review queue") do |(kind, label)| %>
    <%= link_to label, admin_duplicate_bikes_path(search_kind: kind), class: kind == active_kind ? "twlink tw:font-bold" : "twlink" %>
  <% end %>

  <% table.column(label: "Groups") do |(kind, _label)| %>
    <%= number_display(summary.fetch(kind, []).size) %>
  <% end %>

  <% table.column(label: "Registration records") do |(kind, _label)| %>
    <%= number_display(summary.fetch(kind, []).sum { it["record_count"] }) %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<h2 class="tw:mt-6"><%= kinds[@kind] %></h2>

<%= form_with url: admin_duplicate_bikes_path, method: :get, local: true do |form| %>
  <%= form.hidden_field :search_kind, value: @kind %>

  <div class="twfieldrow">
    <%= render UI::Forms::Group::Component.new(form_builder: form, attribute: :search_bike_id, label_text: "Find a registration in this queue", kind: :number_field, html_options: {value: params[:search_bike_id], min: 1}) %>
    <%= render UI::Forms::Group::Component.new(form_builder: form, attribute: :search_organization_id, label_text: "Organization ID (includes initial registration org)", kind: :number_field, html_options: {value: params[:search_organization_id], min: 1}) %>
  </div>

  <%= render UI::Button::Component.new(text: "Filter review queue", color: :primary, type: :submit) %>
<% end %>

<p class="tw:mt-4">
  <%= number_display(@groups_count) %> groups containing
  <%= number_display(@registrations_count) %> registration records in this
  filter.
  <% if @organization %>
    <strong><%= @organization.name %></strong>
  <% end %>
</p>

<%= render Atoms::Admin::PaginationWithCount::Component.new(collection: @groups, index: admin_index_state, count: @groups_count, viewing: "groups") %>
<%= render "review_groups", groups: @groups, representatives: @representatives, organizations: @organizations, kind: @kind %>
<%= render Atoms::Admin::PaginationWithCount::Component.new(collection: @groups, index: admin_index_state, skip_total: true, viewing: "groups") %>
